WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:01.954
India's coal formed in two

2
00:00:01.954 --> 00:00:03.580
very different eras.

3
00:00:03.580 --> 00:00:04.869
Almost all of it is

4
00:00:04.869 --> 00:00:06.388
the older kind.

5
00:00:06.713 --> 00:00:08.675
Gondwana coal is around 200

6
00:00:08.675 --> 00:00:10.091
million years old,

7
00:00:10.091 --> 00:00:12.457
mostly in the Damodar valley.

8
00:00:12.457 --> 00:00:14.074
Tertiary coal is younger,

9
00:00:14.074 --> 00:00:15.999
found in the north-east.

10
00:00:16.345 --> 00:00:18.289
The big fields are Jharia,

11
00:00:18.289 --> 00:00:20.673
Raniganj and Bokaro.

12
00:00:21.018 --> 00:00:23.749
Most Indian coal is bituminous,

13
00:00:23.749 --> 00:00:25.943
and has high ash content.

14
00:00:26.634 --> 00:00:27.905
Your turn.

15
00:00:27.905 --> 00:00:29.631
Where is Jharia?
